cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this guest, cite ANNY and MakeHuman's MPFB2, whose data it reads, and the name sources of unified_expressions.map.
title: headfit.elf -- ANNY head fit and unified-expression transfer (sandbox guest)
abstract: >-
  The host uploads ANNY's data as job data (the guest has no filesystem):
  mpfb2/3dobjs/base.obj, mpfb2/targets/macrodetails (348 targets),
  mpfb2/targets/expression/units (34 units per race), and
  faceunits01/targets/faceunits (52 actions), read directly with no Python.
  local_dials.txt is generated from mpfb2/targets/target.json by
  local_dials.exs. unified_expressions.map takes its 160 names from two
  sources: the VRCFT Unified Expressions animation templates (the
  blendShape names they drive) and the FT_* enum of Godot's
  XRFaceModifier3D, in CamelCase. Only the names are taken; no template
  animation or engine code is copied.
type: software
authors:
  - name: V-Sekai-fire
license: MIT
references:
  - type: data
    title: ANNY faceunits01 (the 52 facial actions, src/anny/data/faceunits01)
    authors:
      - name: NAVER LABS Europe
    repository-code: https://github.com/naver/anny
    commit: fed2f9a23f065dead04fdb180f0b9ebee2ca0b0f
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: >-
      Under ANNY's top-level Apache-2.0 licence, as ANNY distributes it. No
      licence file sits beside the data. Added in b561b37 ("faceunits data",
      2026-06-22) inside mpfb2/ and moved out in e9e0a76. The name matches
      MakeHuman's community faceunits01 asset, so an upstream MakeHuman
      origin (usually CC0) is possible but unconfirmed.
